# Copy to $NORNIR_DOCKER_USER_ROOT/Run/nornir-net-mounts/.run.nornir-net-mounts.env (not committed).
# Shared by start-nornir-build.ps1, run-cursor-dev (net mounts), and worker -DevParityMounts.
# Both NORNIR_NET_*_HOST keys must be set when overriding defaults.
#
# Option A — WSL UNC from PowerShell (Docker Desktop WSL integration ON; exact distro name from wsl -l -v):
#NORNIR_NET_MOUNTS_DIR_HOST=\\wsl.localhost\Ubuntu\mnt\d\Docker\Run\nornir-net-mounts\net-mounts
#NORNIR_NET_CREDS_DIR_HOST=\\wsl.localhost\Ubuntu\mnt\d\Docker\Run\nornir-net-mounts\secrets\net-creds
# Use \\wsl$\Ubuntu\... if \\wsl.localhost\... fails. Wrong distro casing (ubuntu vs Ubuntu) causes distro-services/*.sock errors.
#
# Option B — Windows paths (no WSL UNC; works when integration is off):
#NORNIR_NET_MOUNTS_DIR_HOST=D:\Docker\Run\nornir-net-mounts\net-mounts
#NORNIR_NET_CREDS_DIR_HOST=D:\Docker\Run\nornir-net-mounts\secrets\net-creds
#
# Option C — docker run from a WSL shell:
#NORNIR_NET_MOUNTS_DIR_HOST=/mnt/d/Docker/Run/nornir-net-mounts/net-mounts
#NORNIR_NET_CREDS_DIR_HOST=/mnt/d/Docker/Run/nornir-net-mounts/secrets/net-creds

# Dashboard publishing (NORNIR_MQTT_*) is a nornir-build setting: Run/nornir-build/nornir-build.run.env.
